{"id": "EUVD-2026-64527", "enisaUuid": "13df413b-f2e4-3f68-bf02-17674ec42d22", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nfsverity: Fix bpf_get_fsverity_digest() dynptr assumptions\n\nThe BPF verifier and the dynptr abstraction ensure that the memory space\nreferenced by a dynptr remains valid.  They do not, however, provide any\nguarantee that the contents of the memory are stable.  kfuncs are\nexpected to remain memory-safe even if concurrent modifications occur.\n\nbpf_get_fsverity_digest() didn't follow that: it could crash if\narg->digest_size was concurrently modified.\n\nFix that by using the known-good value hash_alg->digest_size instead.\n\nAlso widen 'dynptr_sz' and 'out_digest_sz' to u64 to match the return\ntype of __bpf_dynptr_size().  It doesn't appear that it can actually be\nmore than INT_MAX currently (since __bpf_dynptr_data_rw() excludes\nfile-based pointers), but the correct type might as well be used.", "datePublished": "2026-08-22T15:31:41", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-16T19:05:59", "baseScore": 7.8, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/1344b632cb5043e32939a84568125719111c5af3", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/2a5cfcad1d56e26d645b7887b0ed24c371851525", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/5bd63cad9df4328a184c409fbdad4f17944bcdb8", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/3e8ec7c0387273329374f5c7bd61f5f38af71fe1"], "aliases": ["GHSA-pxx7-9r2r-m5m2", "CVE-2026-74590"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.13, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "04cfafa3-dbc3-3886-8512-dcbd853dcfe9", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.8"}, {"id": "13e3a795-cd3c-3c46-9874-e4540dd84602", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "67814c00de3161181cddd06c77aeaf86ac4cc584 <2a5cfcad1d56e26d645b7887b0ed24c371851525"}, {"id": "34f4af50-6710-3a12-a8ec-d5c9c84b806e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "67814c00de3161181cddd06c77aeaf86ac4cc584 <1344b632cb5043e32939a84568125719111c5af3"}, {"id": "4a089861-74c5-3124-9e1f-3872299f754f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2"}, {"id": "5340e48c-557d-3295-847d-6584afd655f7", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "67814c00de3161181cddd06c77aeaf86ac4cc584 <5bd63cad9df4328a184c409fbdad4f17944bcdb8"}, {"id": "8137c683-5b45-3b2e-850b-548784c4cc7f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "67814c00de3161181cddd06c77aeaf86ac4cc584 <3e8ec7c0387273329374f5c7bd61f5f38af71fe1"}, {"id": "9d73d9c4-bc82-3681-9faf-6b1431267f35", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.104"}, {"id": "a3037151-08d2-3990-84ea-e7a12dd37bd5", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.45"}, {"id": "bc2a75cc-940d-3108-8816-9453e4ded8ad", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "bfeda836-3a57-3e89-9a7e-b1ca175e83cb", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.1.9"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "46129fdf-0044-3c05-a6bf-6d9bb2512228", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}